From: OpenWrt BPI-R4 Pro PCIe debugging (vendor-derived, NOT upstream)
Subject: [PATCH] clk: mediatek: mt7988: mark pextp_p0..p3_sel clocks as critical

DIAGNOSTIC / VENDOR-DERIVED PATCH. Not upstream, not in 6.18.y.

Port of the pextp part of MediaTek's SDK patch
"999-clk-03-clk-mediatek-mt7988-mark-spi0-and-pextp-clks-as-critical.patch"
(mtk-openwrt-feeds, 25.12 branch) to Linux 6.18. The SPI0 part of the
vendor patch is intentionally NOT included (OpenWrt's
255-clk-mediatek-mt7988-infracfg-SPI0-clocks-are-not-critical.patch
deliberately does the opposite).

CLK_TOP_PEXTP_P0_SEL..CLK_TOP_PEXTP_P3_SEL (topckgen CLK_CFG_13/14) have no
consumer in the mainline MT7988 device tree, so clk_disable_unused()
(late_initcall_sync) gates them if they were left enabled by the boot ROM /
bootloader. The mtk-pcie-gen3 driver probes asynchronously
(PROBE_PREFER_ASYNCHRONOUS) and on BPI-R4 Pro its probe is deferred to the
late_initcall stage, i.e. it may race with clk_disable_unused(). MediaTek
marks these clocks critical in their SDK (and in a later SDK commit also
adds them as "pextp_clk" to the PCIe nodes, "to fix the PCIe issue
happened in PCIe L1ss mode").

Whether this is the root cause of the random "PCIe link down, LTSSM
detect.quiet" on all four ports of BPI-R4 Pro is UNVERIFIED. Test first
with the "clk_ignore_unused" kernel command line argument; keep this
patch only if that measurably helps.

Keeping the clocks ungated costs a negligible amount of power.
---
 drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt7988-topckgen.c | 16 ++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt7988-topckgen.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt7988-topckgen.c
@@ -225,15 +225,15 @@ static const struct mtk_mux top_muxes[] = {
 				   0x0d0, 0x0d4, 0x0d8, 0, 2, 7, 0x1C4, 21, CLK_IS_CRITICAL),
 	MUX_GATE_CLR_SET_UPD_FLAGS(CLK_TOP_INFRA_F26M_SEL, "csw_infra_f26m_sel", sspxtp_parents,
 				   0x0d0, 0x0d4, 0x0d8, 8, 1, 15, 0x1C4, 22, CLK_IS_CRITICAL),
-	MUX_GATE_CLR_SET_UPD(CLK_TOP_PEXTP_P0_SEL, "pextp_p0_sel", sspxtp_parents, 0x0d0, 0x0d4,
-			     0x0d8, 16, 1, 23, 0x1C4, 23),
-	MUX_GATE_CLR_SET_UPD(CLK_TOP_PEXTP_P1_SEL, "pextp_p1_sel", sspxtp_parents, 0x0d0, 0x0d4,
-			     0x0d8, 24, 1, 31, 0x1C4, 24),
+	MUX_GATE_CLR_SET_UPD_FLAGS(CLK_TOP_PEXTP_P0_SEL, "pextp_p0_sel", sspxtp_parents, 0x0d0,
+				   0x0d4, 0x0d8, 16, 1, 23, 0x1C4, 23, CLK_IS_CRITICAL),
+	MUX_GATE_CLR_SET_UPD_FLAGS(CLK_TOP_PEXTP_P1_SEL, "pextp_p1_sel", sspxtp_parents, 0x0d0,
+				   0x0d4, 0x0d8, 24, 1, 31, 0x1C4, 24, CLK_IS_CRITICAL),
 	/* CLK_CFG_14 */
-	MUX_GATE_CLR_SET_UPD(CLK_TOP_PEXTP_P2_SEL, "pextp_p2_sel", sspxtp_parents, 0x0e0, 0x0e4,
-			     0x0e8, 0, 1, 7, 0x1C4, 25),
-	MUX_GATE_CLR_SET_UPD(CLK_TOP_PEXTP_P3_SEL, "pextp_p3_sel", sspxtp_parents, 0x0e0, 0x0e4,
-			     0x0e8, 8, 1, 15, 0x1C4, 26),
+	MUX_GATE_CLR_SET_UPD_FLAGS(CLK_TOP_PEXTP_P2_SEL, "pextp_p2_sel", sspxtp_parents, 0x0e0,
+				   0x0e4, 0x0e8, 0, 1, 7, 0x1C4, 25, CLK_IS_CRITICAL),
+	MUX_GATE_CLR_SET_UPD_FLAGS(CLK_TOP_PEXTP_P3_SEL, "pextp_p3_sel", sspxtp_parents, 0x0e0,
+				   0x0e4, 0x0e8, 8, 1, 15, 0x1C4, 26, CLK_IS_CRITICAL),
 	MUX_GATE_CLR_SET_UPD(CLK_TOP_DA_XTP_GLB_P0_SEL, "da_xtp_glb_p0_sel", da_xtp_glb_p0_parents,
 			     0x0e0, 0x0e4, 0x0e8, 16, 1, 23, 0x1C4, 27),
 	MUX_GATE_CLR_SET_UPD(CLK_TOP_DA_XTP_GLB_P1_SEL, "da_xtp_glb_p1_sel", da_xtp_glb_p0_parents,
